    {
      "id": "PSM-01",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-parabolic-coordinates",
      "title": "Unique coordinates on the stabilizer of an isotropic line",
      "hypotheses": "A CM extension E/F, a hyperbolic pair with pairing one, a nondegenerate Hermitian complement W of rank s and a nonzero trace-zero scalar δ in E.",
      "statement": "The stabilizer is the closed image of (b,z,U,a) ↦ n(b,z)ι(U)m(a). The alternating part of the pairing of the horizontal coordinates contributes [H(b′,b)−H(b,b′)]/(2δ) to the central coordinate of their product.",
