    {
      "id": "PSM-03",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-parabolic-shell-mass",
      "title": "Only the scalar density varies between coordinate shells",
      "hypotheses": "The compact additive and scalar representative sets, a finite-measure fundamental domain for the smaller unitary group, and a real flow of scalar idèles. In the counting application M=s+2≥3.",
      "statement": "For the constructed product shell, its measure is exp(−2d(s+1)j) times the product of the two additive volumes, the complementary quotient covolume and the weighted integral over the compact idèle set. After the scalar count the remaining geometric ratio is exp(−2ds).",
